# Text files are stored and checked out with LF line endings on every host.
# A Windows checkout with core.autocrlf=true turned the bridge lists and the
# Tor binary pin file into CRLF, which made a Play bundle built there differ
# from the F-Droid APK built on Linux in exactly those entries.
* text=auto eol=lf
*.sh text eol=lf
*.py text eol=lf
*.gradle text eol=lf
*.properties text eol=lf
*.xml text eol=lf
*.java text eol=lf
*.kt text eol=lf
*.md text eol=lf
*.yml text eol=lf
*.sha256 text eol=lf
bridges-* text eol=lf
gradlew text eol=lf
gradlew.bat text eol=crlf

# Binary inputs are never normalised.
*.jar binary
*.so binary
*.a binary
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.webp binary
*.gif binary
*.mp4 binary
*.ogg binary
*.opus binary
*.zip binary
*.apk binary
*.aab binary
*.keystore binary
*.jks binary
*.gpg binary
*.kbx binary
*.ttf binary
*.otf binary
